      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "pageStart": 13,
      "pageEnd": 13,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "# Introduction\n\nSubstandard and falsified medical products pose a multilayered threat to the stability of health systems. They endanger health, through either therapeutic failure or adverse effects, and they undermine public trust in health care. They also risk jeopardizing global efforts working to suppress antimicrobial resistance, threatening the long-term efficacy of key life-saving medicines. Further to their impacts on health, substandard and falsified medical products have adverse socioeconomic consequences and increase poverty by damaging individual productivity, income and social mobi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the public health, antimicrobial resistance, and socioeconomic threats posed by substandard and falsified medical products, states the agreed WHO/Member State definitions, explains how supply chain complexity and procurement pressures increase risk in LMICs, and highlights the role of risk-based post-market surveillance (Rb-PMS) and NMRAs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "antigravity",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789240120747-eng/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Reporting of substandard and falsified medical products",
      "pageStart": 13,
      "pageEnd": 14,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-reporting-of-substandard-and-falsified-medical-p.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "## Reporting of substandard and falsified medical products\n\nReporting suspected substandard and falsified medical products allows NMRAs to investigate them more thoroughly than the reporter. When a case of a substandard and falsified medical product is confirmed, relevant authorities can quickly remove the product from the supply chain and market, impose sanctions and address system weaknesses. In the long term, this should improve product quality and reduce the chances of substandard and falsified medical products entering the market (27).\n\nIn addition to reducing prevalence at a national lev",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains how reporting suspected substandard and falsified medical products enables NMRA investigation, market removal, and global surveillance via the WHO Global Surveillance and Monitoring System (GSMS), notes the frontline role and under-reporting of health care professionals, and motivates transitioning from paper-based reporting to standards-based digital solutions such as smartphone applications piloted in Indonesia and the United Republic of Tanzania.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "antigravity",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789240120747-eng/blocks/prose-sec-005",
